-- BREACH-DOCTOR-1 v1 (2026-10-26, charter pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000266, with 100360 and the CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1 / CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1 family).
-- Owner, 2026-10-24 and again 2026-10-26: "FLEET IS NOT SELF-DIAGNOSING ITS OWN BREACHES AND AUTOMATICALLY REMEDIATING". Measured 2026-10-26 06:36Z on qnfo-audit:
-- 447 open agent_issues, 371 with no doer in v_issue_age_ladder; the code planner marks them untrusted or not-code and no other loop owns the diagnosis of a family.
-- BREACH-SELFHEAL-1 (a D1 trigger on fleet_tick) was dropped by FLEET-TICK-SPLIT-1 (it caused the SQLITE_NOMEM heartbeat outage), so the doctor is WORKER CODE:
-- qnfo-fleet-control breachDoctorTick (0.52.0) on the */10 slot. This file is the data it reads and writes. It adds no D1 trigger, and none on fleet_tick (S7).
--
-- WHAT THE ENGINE DOES WITH THESE TABLES (qnfo-fleet-control/worker.js, block BREACH-DOCTOR-1)
--   S1  Playbooks are data. breach_playbooks.trigger_sql and verify_sql are one read-only SELECT each (the remediation tick's write-keyword guard). Each action_sql / revert_sql
--       statement is exactly one INSERT or UPDATE on issue_triage, agent_issues (UPDATE only), remediation_contracts, issue_plans, ops_config or human_actions, binds ?1 = the
--       issue id, has no semicolon, no DELETE/DROP/ALTER/CREATE/PRAGMA/ATTACH, no INSERT INTO agent_issues or code_tasks, and names no free-text column (description,
--       exceptions_json, cloud_ops_events text/meta; the taint rule: free text never flows into an issue, a probe, a task or a prompt). A rule that fails validation is skipped
--       with a taint-drop event and counted in doctor_taint_violations_24h.
--   S2  Action kinds are closed in code: sql (the validated statements), file-issue (title BREACH-DOCTOR-1: <rule> <subject>, constant description, deduped on the open title)
--       and owner-card (a human_actions row whose why carries IDENTITY-BOUND: <enum reason>, a default in effect and a closing probe). No model call in v1 (breach_doctor_ai = off).
--   S3  A playbook younger than breach_doctor_playbook_cooldown_min (30) runs in measure (the would-do diagnosis only); a rule with 2 or more failed or reverted cases in 24 hours
--       demotes itself to measure; max_per_tick and max_per_day per rule; a live work claim on issue:<id> skips the case; every applied action stores its revert_sql in the ledger
--       and writes a decision_log row and a breach_diagnosis_events row; lease_until is never more than 120 minutes ahead and is renewed only by a progress event.
--       An issue whose last case failed is retried after 60 minutes; after 3 failed or reverted cases it is retried at most once in 120 minutes (a rate with a release, never a
--       permanent exclusion: control breach-doctor-strike-cap) and the self issue BREACH-DOCTOR-1: self <rule> <code> is filed once for a fix of the playbook row.
--   S4  Every unowned open issue older than breach_doctor_min_age_min (120 minutes, SLA-120M-1: action starts at the first tick past 120 minutes; bounds 10..120) is classified
--       (family from a code table of title prefixes, cause_class from the playbook that matched or unclassified, facts_json from numbers, ids and enum codes only), critical
--       first, up to breach_doctor_max_cases a tick. An issue titled BREACH-DOCTOR-1: (a gap or a self issue) is classified and counted like any other (family BREACH-DOCTOR-1,
--       cause unclassified) but takes no playbook hit and no action (control breach-doctor-own-issue-guard), so the doctor cannot act on its own issues and cannot hide them
--       from its own metric. breaches_undiagnosed_over_60m counts an issue until a case FOUND its cause (cause_class other than unclassified): classification coverage is not a diagnosis.
--       The generic playbook-gap row is seeded in MEASURE and files nothing (review 2026-10-26): a gap issue carries no code-task or code-anchor line (the lever for a family is a NEW
--       breach_playbooks row by migration, not an edit of an existing file), so the code loop has nothing to edit and the issue would only add an unowned issue to the backlog the doctor
--       drains (a fixture shaped like live filed 19 gap issues in 7 ticks, none with a doer). The gap is still recorded by family: each case of an unmatched family is a breach_diagnoses
--       row with cause_class unclassified, v_breach_doctor_status reports unclassified_cases, gap_families and gap_by_family, and breaches_undiagnosed_over_60m keeps counting those issues
--       (its metric trigger already routes the lever to a trusted METRIC-TRIGGER- issue). The doctor's own self issue (3 failed cases of one issue) is the only issue it files by itself.
--       The switch that files gap issues (control breach-doctor-gap-measure): UPDATE breach_playbooks SET mode = 'on' WHERE rule_id = 'playbook-gap', by migration with its decision_log row.
--       Armed, the engine files one "BREACH-DOCTOR-1: playbook gap <family>" issue per family per 24 hours, never for OWNER-CHAT, OWNER-REQUEST, other or BREACH-DOCTOR-1 (owner prose, a
--       catch-all and the doctor's own issues, which no playbook can close), and none while 3 gap issues are open. The second migration, migrations/2026-10-26-breach-doctor-trust.sql,
--       adds the single pair qnfo-fleet-control|BREACH-DOCTOR-1: to ops_config code_merge_trusted_sources so the planner reads the doctor's titles as trusted; before it applies, the
--       description of any issue the doctor files says "Doer: none yet" instead of naming the code loop.
--   S5  Verify reads verify_sql of an applied case: two consecutive passes are verified, a failed verify is failed (error_code, attempts + 1), 3 failures file a self issue. A case in
--       queued, applied or verifying whose lease has run out is failed lease-expired by the same phase (it runs in on and in measure; breach_doctor = off writes nothing, so queue_sla
--       row breach-doctor-case-in-flight and the contract fm-breach-doctor-case-age watch the oldest in-flight case at 120 minutes, QUEUE-SLA-1).
--   S6  The metrics are written first in every tick, by worker code, so a dead heartbeat cannot hide. Single flight: loop_lock k = breach-doctor, ttl 4 minutes. ops_config
--       breach_doctor = off returns before any write. The tick has a wall budget (breach_doctor_budget_ms) and reads about 10,500 rows (6,300 of state, 4,000 for the four CM triggers and 250 for the facts of 40 cases, measured on live D1 2026-10-26 10:02Z, the largest statement 4,023; it never reads v_issue_age_ladder, 211,166 rows).
--   S7  No D1 trigger on fleet_tick and no trigger chain.
--
-- COVERAGE RE-VERIFIED 2026-10-26 10:02Z (live D1, SELECT only). ISSUE-HYGIENE-1 (qnfo-github-steward 0.8.0, migrations/2026-10-26-issue-hygiene-1.sql) merged between the audit
-- and this file: its hourly D1 workflow issue-meta-fold already closed the 10 CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1 issues whose task merged and the 7 CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1 issues whose definition
-- of done was met (close_channel workflow:ISSUE-HYGIENE-1), and a session sweep of the same workflow closed the twin 100382 as superseded by 100392 at 09:34Z. The four seed triggers
-- below therefore read 0 rows on live qnfo-audit today (399, 405, 1,612 and 1,550 rows read): the doctor takes no action on its first tick, and none in its 30 minutes of measure
-- either way. They are the same facts read every 10 minutes by the doctor: the second path (a faster one than the hourly workflow once an issue is 120 minutes old), the guard if that workflow
-- stops, and the end-to-end proof of the engine. The fixtures of migrations/breach-doctor.test.mjs reproduce the live shapes (the 100382/100392 twin included) and prove each rule.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE ops_config SET value = 'off' WHERE key = 'breach_doctor'; UPDATE breach_playbooks SET enabled = 0, mode = 'measure'; DROP VIEW IF EXISTS v_breach_doctor_status; DROP VIEW IF EXISTS v_breach_owner; DROP VIEW IF EXISTS v_breach_diagnosis_current; DELETE FROM analytics_metric_triggers WHERE metric_key IN ('breaches_undiagnosed_over_60m', 'breaches_auto_remediated_24h', 'doctor_actions_failed_24h', 'doctor_tick_age_min', 'doctor_taint_violations_24h'); DELETE FROM metric_registry WHERE metric IN ('breaches_undiagnosed_over_60m', 'breaches_auto_remediated_24h', 'doctor_actions_failed_24h', 'doctor_tick_age_min', 'doctor_taint_violations_24h'); DELETE FROM ops_config WHERE key LIKE 'breach_doctor_%'; DELETE FROM control_registry WHERE control LIKE 'breach-doctor-%'; DELETE FROM spof_registry WHERE component LIKE 'breach doctor%'; DELETE FROM belief_registry WHERE belief_key = 'belief-doctor-structured-facts-suffice'; DELETE FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class IN ('belief-doctor-structured-facts-suffice', 'fm-breach-doctor-stalled', 'fm-breach-doctor-rule-demoted', 'fm-breach-doctor-case-age'); DELETE FROM failure_modes WHERE fm_key IN ('breach-doctor-stalled', 'breach-doctor-rule-demoted', 'breach-doctor-case-age'); DELETE FROM queue_sla WHERE stuck_type = 'breach-doctor-case-in-flight'; DELETE FROM capability_ledger WHERE capability = 'breach-doctor:remediate-unowned-breaches'; DELETE FROM metric_breach_cause WHERE note = 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1'; DELETE FROM breach_causes WHERE cause_key = 'breach-doctor' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM metric_breach_cause WHERE cause_key = 'breach-doctor'); the three breach_* tables stay as the ledger (breach_doctor = off stops the engine), the three BREACH-DOCTOR-*-1 issues and their issue-<id> contracts stay (an issue is closed only with close_evidence) and the decision_log row stays (append-only).
-- spof-review: no new cron, worker or binding. The engine rides qnfo-fleet-control's */10 slot; its second path (qnfo-cloud-ops jobBreachDoctorWatch, reading doctor_tick_age_min) is the issue BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 filed below, and the spof_registry row points at it.
-- charter-pillar: autonomy. Table family +3 (breach_diagnoses, breach_diagnosis_events, breach_playbooks); the writers of breach_selfheal_actions and issue_age_replans (the D1 triggers breach_selfheal_heavy_tick and deploy_merge_age_tick) are retired by the issue BREACH-DOCTOR-RETIRE-1 filed below, with its probe (both tables stay readable).

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS breach_diagnoses (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  issue_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
  case_key TEXT NOT NULL,
  family TEXT NOT NULL,
  rule_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  rule_version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
  cause_class TEXT NOT NULL,
  facts_json TEXT NOT NULL,
  evidence_hash TEXT NOT NULL,
  confidence TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'rule' CHECK (confidence IN ('rule', 'rule+model')),
  model TEXT,
  action_kind TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'none' CHECK (action_kind IN ('none', 'sql', 'file-issue', 'owner-card')),
  action_ref TEXT,
  revert_sql TEXT,
  state TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'diagnosed' CHECK (state IN ('diagnosed', 'queued', 'applied', 'verifying', 'verified', 'failed', 'reverted', 'handed-owner', 'superseded')),
  verify_class TEXT,
  mode TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'on' CHECK (mode IN ('measure', 'on')),
  attempts INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
  verify_passes INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
  error_code TEXT,
  opened_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')),
  diagnosed_at TEXT,
  applied_at TEXT,
  verified_at TEXT,
  last_progress_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')),
  lease_until TEXT,
  tick_id TEXT
);
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS uq_breach_diag_live ON breach_diagnoses (issue_id) WHERE state NOT IN ('verified', 'superseded', 'reverted', 'failed');
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_breach_diag_state_lease ON breach_diagnoses (state, lease_until);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_breach_diag_case ON breach_diagnoses (case_key, state);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_breach_diag_issue ON breach_diagnoses (issue_id, opened_at);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_breach_diag_rule_ts ON breach_diagnoses (rule_id, state, last_progress_at);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS breach_diagnosis_events (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  ts TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')),
  issue_id INTEGER,
  diagnosis_id INTEGER,
  event TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (event IN ('requested', 'selected', 'diagnosed', 'action', 'verify', 'renew', 'handoff', 'fail', 'revert', 'supersede', 'taint-drop', 'budget-skip', 'skip', 'demote', 'tick')),
  from_state TEXT,
  to_state TEXT,
  detail TEXT,
  tick_id TEXT
);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_breach_diag_events_issue ON breach_diagnosis_events (issue_id, ts);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_breach_diag_events_kind ON breach_diagnosis_events (event, ts);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS breach_playbooks (
  rule_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
  family TEXT NOT NULL,
  cause_class TEXT NOT NULL,
  action_kind TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'sql' CHECK (action_kind IN ('sql', 'file-issue', 'owner-card')),
  trigger_sql TEXT NOT NULL,
  action_sql TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]' CHECK (json_valid(action_sql)),
  revert_sql TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]' CHECK (json_valid(revert_sql)),
  verify_sql TEXT NOT NULL,
  min_ladder TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'delegated',
  max_per_tick INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 3,
  max_per_day INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 12,
  enabled INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
  mode TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'measure' CHECK (mode IN ('measure', 'on')),
  created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')),
  note TEXT
);

CREATE VIEW IF NOT EXISTS v_breach_diagnosis_current AS
SELECT d.* FROM breach_diagnoses d
WHERE d.id = (SELECT MAX(x.id) FROM breach_diagnoses x WHERE x.issue_id = d.issue_id);

CREATE VIEW IF NOT EXISTS v_breach_owner AS
SELECT a.id AS issue_id,
  CASE
    WHEN instr(COALESCE(a.description, ''), 'code-task:') > 0 THEN 'code-task line'
    WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM code_tasks k WHERE k.goal LIKE '[issue #' || a.id || ']%' AND k.status NOT IN ('failed', 'closed', 'superseded', 'needs_human')) THEN 'live code task'
    WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM work_claims w WHERE (w.issue_id = a.id OR w.path = 'issue:' || a.id) AND w.released_at IS NULL AND w.expires_at > strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')) THEN 'live work claim'
    WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_diagnoses d WHERE d.issue_id = a.id AND d.mode = 'on' AND d.state IN ('queued', 'applied', 'verifying')
                   AND d.action_ref IS NOT NULL AND d.action_kind <> 'none'
                   AND d.lease_until > strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')
                   AND d.last_progress_at > strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now', '-120 minutes')) THEN 'breach doctor'
    WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM breach_diagnoses d WHERE d.issue_id = a.id AND d.state = 'handed-owner' AND d.action_kind = 'owner-card'
                   AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM human_actions h WHERE h.slug = d.action_ref AND h.status = 'open' AND instr(COALESCE(h.why, ''), 'IDENTITY-BOUND:') > 0)) THEN 'owner card (identity-bound)'
    ELSE NULL END AS owner_kind
FROM agent_issues a WHERE a.status = 'open';

CREATE VIEW IF NOT EXISTS v_breach_doctor_status AS
SELECT
  COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = 'breach_doctor'), 'measure') AS mode,
  COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = 'breach_doctor_ai'), 'off') AS ai,
  (SELECT MAX(ts) FROM breach_diagnosis_events WHERE event = 'tick') AS last_tick_at,
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM breach_diagnoses WHERE opened_at > strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now', '-24 hours')) AS cases_24h,
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM breach_diagnoses WHERE state = 'verified' AND verified_at > strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now', '-24 hours')) AS verified_24h,
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM breach_diagnoses WHERE state IN ('failed', 'reverted') AND last_progress_at > strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now', '-24 hours')) AS failed_24h,
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM breach_diagnoses WHERE state IN ('queued', 'applied', 'verifying')) AS in_flight,
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM breach_diagnoses WHERE state IN ('queued', 'applied', 'verifying') AND lease_until < strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')) AS lease_expired,
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM breach_diagnosis_events WHERE event = 'taint-drop' AND ts > strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now', '-24 hours')) AS taint_drops_24h,
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM v_breach_diagnosis_current WHERE state = 'diagnosed' AND cause_class = 'unclassified') AS unclassified_cases,
  (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT family) FROM v_breach_diagnosis_current WHERE state = 'diagnosed' AND cause_class = 'unclassified') AS gap_families,
  (SELECT group_concat(g.family || ':' || g.n, ' ') FROM (SELECT family, COUNT(*) AS n FROM v_breach_diagnosis_current WHERE state = 'diagnosed' AND cause_class = 'unclassified' GROUP BY family ORDER BY n DESC, family LIMIT 12) g) AS gap_by_family;

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO ops_config (key, value, note) VALUES
 ('breach_doctor', 'on', 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: on = diagnose and act; measure = diagnose and record the would-do, act on nothing; off = stop, before any write (migrations/2026-10-26-breach-doctor.sql). Tri-state, read by bdConfig(): a missing or unreadable value means measure.'),
 ('breach_doctor_ai', 'off', 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: v1 makes no model call; the switch is reserved. A breached ai_spend cap routes to the cheapest model and fewer calls, never to a stop (BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1).'),
 ('breach_doctor_max_cases', '40', 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: issues classified per 10-minute tick (1..60). 334 open issues were older than 120 minutes on 2026-10-26 (318 older than 8 hours, 81 with a code-task line), so 40 a tick drain the unowned ones in under 9 ticks, inside the 120-minute SLA.'),
 ('breach_doctor_max_actions', '6', 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: state-changing actions per tick (0..20), backpressure, never a stop'),
 ('breach_doctor_budget_ms', '20000', 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: wall budget per tick in ms (5000..40000); no new case starts after 85% of it'),
 ('breach_doctor_min_age_min', '120', 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: an open issue with no doer becomes a case from this age in minutes (10..120, SLA-120M-1: no SLA exceeds 120 minutes and action starts at the first tick past it), so the 24 h breach never forms'),
 ('breach_doctor_playbook_cooldown_min', '30', 'BREACH-DOCTOR-1: a playbook younger than this many minutes (0..120) runs in measure and writes the would-do diagnosis only');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO breach_playbooks (rule_id, version, family, cause_class, action_kind, trigger_sql, action_sql, revert_sql, verify_sql, min_ladder, max_per_tick, max_per_day, enabled, mode, note) VALUES
  ('CM-R1', 1, 'CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1', 'merged-after-refusal', 'sql', 'SELECT a.id AS issue_id, ''merged-after-refusal'' AS subject, json_object(''task_id'', t.id, ''pr_number'', l.pr_number, ''pr_state'', COALESCE(l.pr_state, ''none''), ''merged_at'', t.merged_at, ''merged_sha7'', substr(t.merged_sha, 1, 7), ''merged_by'', t.merged_by) AS facts_json FROM agent_issues a JOIN code_tasks t ON t.id = substr(a.title, instr(a.title, ''code task '') + 10, instr(substr(a.title, instr(a.title, ''code task '') + 10) || '' '', '' '') - 1) LEFT JOIN code_task_pr_links l ON l.task_id = t.id WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND a.title LIKE ''CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1: code task ct_%'' AND t.status = ''merged'' AND t.merged_sha IS NOT NULL AND t.merged_at IS NOT NULL AND COALESCE(l.pr_state, ''merged'') = ''merged'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM work_claims w WHERE (w.issue_id = a.id OR w.path = ''issue:'' || a.id) AND w.released_at IS NULL AND w.expires_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now''))', json_array('INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence) SELECT a.id, ''breach-doctor:CM-R1'', ''closed'', ''breach-doctor'', datetime(''now''), ''DoD met: code task '' || t.id || '' status=merged ('' || COALESCE(''PR #'' || l.pr_number || '' '' || l.pr_state, ''PR '' || COALESCE(t.pr_url, ''?'')) || '', merged_at '' || t.merged_at || '', merge sha '' || substr(t.merged_sha, 1, 7) || '', merged_by '' || COALESCE(t.merged_by, ''?'') || ''). The merge runner refused the pull request on a required check before this merge, so the refusal no longer applies. Closed by breach-doctor rule CM-R1 from code_tasks and code_task_pr_links facts only.'' FROM agent_issues a JOIN code_tasks t ON t.id = substr(a.title, instr(a.title, ''code task '') + 10, instr(substr(a.title, instr(a.title, ''code task '') + 10) || '' '', '' '') - 1) LEFT JOIN code_task_pr_links l ON l.task_id = t.id WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND a.title LIKE ''CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1: code task ct_%'' AND t.status = ''merged'' AND t.merged_sha IS NOT NULL AND t.merged_at IS NOT NULL AND COALESCE(l.pr_state, ''merged'') = ''merged'' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM work_claims w WHERE (w.issue_id = a.id OR w.path = ''issue:'' || a.id) AND w.released_at IS NULL AND w.expires_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'')) AND a.id = ?1 ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = ''closed'', owner = ''breach-doctor'', close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence'), json_array('UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = ''triaged'', close_evidence = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1', 'UPDATE agent_issues SET status = ''open'', close_channel = NULL, updated_at = CAST(strftime(''%s'',''now'') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''closed'''), 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = ?1 AND status IN (''closed'',''resolved'')) THEN ''issue-reopened'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues a JOIN code_tasks t ON t.id = substr(a.title, instr(a.title, ''code task '') + 10, instr(substr(a.title, instr(a.title, ''code task '') + 10) || '' '', '' '') - 1) WHERE a.id = ?1 AND t.status = ''merged'') THEN ''ok'' ELSE ''task-not-merged'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 12, 40, 1, 'on', 'CODE-MERGE-REFUSED-1 whose code task has since merged (10 open on 2026-10-26 06:36Z, every one merged 0.6 to 60 h after the refusal). Closes with close_evidence naming the task, PR and merge sha. Verify measures the task, not the guarded issue. The hourly issue-meta-fold workflow (ISSUE-HYGIENE-1) closed those 10 at 06:51Z, so this rule has no live hit; it is the 10-minute second path and the guard if that workflow stops.'),
  ('CM-R2', 1, 'CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1', 'source-issue-closed', 'sql', 'WITH e AS (SELECT a.id AS issue_id, t.id AS task_id, t.status AS tstatus, t.step AS step, t.attempts AS attempts, t.created_at AS tcreated, CASE WHEN t.goal LIKE ''[issue #%'' THEN CAST(substr(t.goal, 9, instr(t.goal, '']'') - 9) AS INTEGER) WHEN t.id LIKE ''ct_im%'' THEN CAST(substr(t.id, 6) AS INTEGER) END AS parent_id FROM agent_issues a JOIN code_tasks t ON t.id = substr(a.title, 24, instr(substr(a.title, 24) || '' '', '' '') - 1) WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND a.title LIKE ''CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1: ct_% %'') SELECT e.issue_id AS issue_id, ''source-issue-closed'' AS subject, json_object(''task_id'', e.task_id, ''task_status'', e.tstatus, ''task_step'', e.step, ''task_attempts'', e.attempts, ''parent_id'', pa.id, ''parent_status'', pa.status) AS facts_json FROM e JOIN agent_issues pa ON pa.id = e.parent_id JOIN issue_triage pt ON pt.issue_id = pa.id JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = e.issue_id WHERE pa.status IN (''closed'',''resolved'') AND TRIM(COALESCE(pt.close_evidence, '''')) <> '''' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM work_claims w WHERE (w.issue_id = a.id OR w.path = ''issue:'' || a.id) AND w.released_at IS NULL AND w.expires_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now''))', json_array('WITH e AS (SELECT a.id AS issue_id, t.id AS task_id, t.status AS tstatus, t.step AS step, t.attempts AS attempts, t.created_at AS tcreated, CASE WHEN t.goal LIKE ''[issue #%'' THEN CAST(substr(t.goal, 9, instr(t.goal, '']'') - 9) AS INTEGER) WHEN t.id LIKE ''ct_im%'' THEN CAST(substr(t.id, 6) AS INTEGER) END AS parent_id FROM agent_issues a JOIN code_tasks t ON t.id = substr(a.title, 24, instr(substr(a.title, 24) || '' '', '' '') - 1) WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND a.title LIKE ''CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1: ct_% %'') INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence) SELECT a.id, ''breach-doctor:CM-R2'', ''closed'', ''breach-doctor'', datetime(''now''), ''DoD moot: the task''''s source issue #'' || pa.id || '' is '' || pa.status || '' (close_channel '' || COALESCE(pa.close_channel, ''none'') || '', at '' || datetime(pa.updated_at / 1000, ''unixepoch'') || ''Z) and carries its own close evidence'' || COALESCE('' ('' || CASE WHEN pt.close_evidence GLOB ''remediation_verifications#[0-9]*'' THEN substr(pt.close_evidence, 1, instr(pt.close_evidence || '' '', '' '') - 1) END || '')'', '''') || ''. Code task '' || e.task_id || '' ended '' || e.tstatus || '' at step '' || e.step || '' after '' || e.attempts || '' attempts with no change of its own to land. Closed by breach-doctor rule CM-R2 from agent_issues, issue_triage and code_tasks facts only.'' FROM e JOIN agent_issues pa ON pa.id = e.parent_id JOIN issue_triage pt ON pt.issue_id = pa.id JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = e.issue_id WHERE pa.status IN (''closed'',''resolved'') AND TRIM(COALESCE(pt.close_evidence, '''')) <> '''' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM work_claims w WHERE (w.issue_id = a.id OR w.path = ''issue:'' || a.id) AND w.released_at IS NULL AND w.expires_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'')) AND a.id = ?1 ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = ''closed'', owner = ''breach-doctor'', close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence'), json_array('UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = ''triaged'', close_evidence = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1', 'UPDATE agent_issues SET status = ''open'', close_channel = NULL, updated_at = CAST(strftime(''%s'',''now'') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''closed'''), 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = ?1 AND status IN (''closed'',''resolved'')) THEN ''issue-reopened'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues x JOIN code_tasks t ON t.id = substr(x.title, 24, instr(substr(x.title, 24) || '' '', '' '') - 1) JOIN agent_issues pa ON pa.id = CASE WHEN t.goal LIKE ''[issue #%'' THEN CAST(substr(t.goal, 9, instr(t.goal, '']'') - 9) AS INTEGER) WHEN t.id LIKE ''ct_im%'' THEN CAST(substr(t.id, 6) AS INTEGER) END WHERE x.id = ?1 AND pa.status IN (''closed'',''resolved'')) THEN ''ok'' ELSE ''source-issue-open'' END AS observed', 'delegated', 12, 40, 1, 'on', 'CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1 whose source issue was closed with its own evidence (6 open on 2026-10-26 06:36Z). A wontfix parent is a decision and is excluded. issue-meta-fold (ISSUE-HYGIENE-1) closed those 6 at 06:51Z (code-loop-exhausted-dod-met): this rule is the 10-minute second path.'),
  ('CM-R3', 1, 'CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1', 'duplicate-exhaustion', 'sql', 'WITH e AS (SELECT a.id AS issue_id, t.id AS task_id, t.status AS tstatus, t.step AS step, t.attempts AS attempts, t.created_at AS tcreated, CASE WHEN t.goal LIKE ''[issue #%'' THEN CAST(substr(t.goal, 9, instr(t.goal, '']'') - 9) AS INTEGER) WHEN t.id LIKE ''ct_im%'' THEN CAST(substr(t.id, 6) AS INTEGER) END AS parent_id FROM agent_issues a JOIN code_tasks t ON t.id = substr(a.title, 24, instr(substr(a.title, 24) || '' '', '' '') - 1) WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND a.title LIKE ''CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1: ct_% %'') SELECT e.issue_id AS issue_id, ''duplicate-exhaustion'' AS subject, json_object(''task_id'', e.task_id, ''parent_id'', e.parent_id, ''successor_issue'', nt.issue_id, ''successor_task'', nt.task_id) AS facts_json FROM e JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = e.issue_id JOIN e nt ON nt.parent_id = e.parent_id AND nt.issue_id = (SELECT MAX(x.issue_id) FROM e x WHERE x.parent_id = e.parent_id) WHERE e.parent_id IS NOT NULL AND e.issue_id <> nt.issue_id AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM work_claims w WHERE (w.issue_id = a.id OR w.path = ''issue:'' || a.id) AND w.released_at IS NULL AND w.expires_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now''))', json_array('WITH e AS (SELECT a.id AS issue_id, t.id AS task_id, t.status AS tstatus, t.step AS step, t.attempts AS attempts, t.created_at AS tcreated, CASE WHEN t.goal LIKE ''[issue #%'' THEN CAST(substr(t.goal, 9, instr(t.goal, '']'') - 9) AS INTEGER) WHEN t.id LIKE ''ct_im%'' THEN CAST(substr(t.id, 6) AS INTEGER) END AS parent_id FROM agent_issues a JOIN code_tasks t ON t.id = substr(a.title, 24, instr(substr(a.title, 24) || '' '', '' '') - 1) WHERE a.status = ''open'' AND a.title LIKE ''CODE-LOOP-EXHAUSTED-1: ct_% %'') INSERT INTO issue_triage (issue_id, rc, triage_state, owner, sla_due_at, close_evidence) SELECT a.id, ''breach-doctor:CM-R3'', ''closed'', ''breach-doctor'', datetime(''now''), ''SUPERSEDED BY #'' || nt.issue_id || '': both issues report the exhausted code loop for the same source issue #'' || e.parent_id || '' (tasks '' || e.task_id || '' and '' || nt.task_id || ''), #'' || nt.issue_id || '' stays open and carries the work. Closed by breach-doctor rule CM-R3 from agent_issues and code_tasks facts only.'' FROM e JOIN agent_issues a ON a.id = e.issue_id JOIN e nt ON nt.parent_id = e.parent_id AND nt.issue_id = (SELECT MAX(x.issue_id) FROM e x WHERE x.parent_id = e.parent_id) WHERE e.parent_id IS NOT NULL AND e.issue_id <> nt.issue_id AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM remediation_contracts c WHERE c.issue_id = a.id AND c.status IN (''active'',''holding'') AND COALESCE(c.last_verdict,'''') IN (''fail'',''vacuous-probe-result'',''probe-error'',''probe-not-machine-executable'',''probe-same-account-host'')) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM work_claims w WHERE (w.issue_id = a.id OR w.path = ''issue:'' || a.id) AND w.released_at IS NULL AND w.expires_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'',''now'')) AND a.id = ?1 ON CONFLICT(issue_id) DO UPDATE SET rc = excluded.rc, triage_state = ''closed'', owner = ''breach-doctor'', close_evidence = excluded.close_evidence'), json_array('UPDATE issue_triage SET triage_state = ''triaged'', close_evidence = NULL WHERE issue_id = ?1', 'UPDATE agent_issues SET status = ''open'', close_channel = NULL, updated_at = CAST(strftime(''%s'',''now'') AS INTEGER) * 1000 WHERE id = ?1 AND status = ''closed'''), 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE id = ?1 AND status IN (''closed'',''resolved'')) THEN ''issue-reopened'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM issue_triage it JOIN agent_issues s ON s.id = CAST(substr(it.close_evidence, 16) AS INTEGER) WHERE it.issue_id = ?1 AND it.close_evidence LIKE ''SUPERS